==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Masai Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Jiangshi Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Pogo Cat exists mainly to take hits in place of other units, like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]]. The difference comes from Pogo Cat costing a lot more, but being able to survive anyone's attacks thanks to his Survive ability. In practice, his cost isn't worth the resulting effect, making his use recommended only as a replacement for [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] in stages with an overabundance of money.

This unit also delivers high damage for what he is, which allows him to be more desirable as a meatshield in certain occasions, but it is usually much better to let Tank Cat defend and your attackers of choice do the damage.

The most notable Cat Combo that Pogo has is named ''Tiny Ancient Hunt,'' with [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Dragon Cat]]. It proves as a great combo as not only does it give an small attack buff for only 2 slots, but both the units in the combo are actually useful in battle (most of the time). The other cat combo, ''Pyon Pyon for Two,'' is not as usable as the other the previous Cat Combo mentioned, but it has its uses in metal stages for example.

==='''True Form'''===
Jiangshi Cat becomes much better at what he does, as he can now survive attacks every time and costs less. Although he is still too expensive to be used on everyday situations, he can become a valuable asset in situations where units have no chance of tanking hits, or where holding the position becomes important.

He shines on levels where enemies drop tons of money or have slow, long range hitters, such as [[Dark Emperor Nyandam|Nyandam]] or [[THE SLOTH]], against whom he can pile up damage while guaranteeing some sort of defense line stay after the attack. He is also good on most [[:Category:Cyclone Stages|Cyclone stages]], as every meatshield will only survive one hit anyways.

==='''Talents'''===
The story changes when this unit receives talents. Speed is the most important, as it allows Jiangshi to get in the way of enemies way more easily, plus he can hope to deliver his pretty good DPS on slow hitters for far longer. This makes him more aggressive and better at keeping the enemies busy. Damage and health up are good talents if your Jiangshi has a decent level, as they allow him to survive attacks and leave a bigger impact with his attacks more often, but going further than level 5 may not be worth it. Resist slow is a good improvement that extends Jiangshi's usability, especially since the effect would likely run out while he's being knocked back in most cases, causing it to act like an immunity.

The Resist Wave talent will rarely come into play, unless one owns a Resist Wave S orb, turning Jiangshi into a Wave Immune meatshield, otherwise, simply reducing wave damage is pointless since the Survive ability leaves Jiangshi at 1 health.

==='''Orb'''===
A Cash Back orb is a great choice if want to make Jiangshi put less of a strain of your wallet. Dodge Attack orb works very well with Survive, giving him even more survivability.

