==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.4 Update|Version 2.0.4]] reduced Pogo Cat's attack rate from 54f<sup>1.8s</sup> to 49f<sup>1.63s</sup>.
*[[Version 4.0 Update|Version 4.0]] gave Pogo Cat the Survive ability.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Pogo Cat was a part of six other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Boing Boing (Removed Combo)|Boing Boing]], [[Cosplayers (Removed Combo)|Cosplayers]], [[With a View (Removed Combo)|With a View]], [[Nostalgia (Removed Combo)|Nostalgia]], [[Face Paint (Removed Combo)|Face Paint]] and [[Valorous (Removed Combo)|Valorous]].
**If all of its combos had been kept, Pogo Cat would be tied with [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] for having the most Cat Combos in the game.
*Prior to [[Version 10.8 Update|Version 10.8]], Pogo Cat was also in [[Little Warriors (Combo)|Little Warriors]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Pogo Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Pogo Cat
Sucked in to the recent (?) trend of toys.
Still, looks pretty fun.
Cheap to produce, might survive being broken.</pre>
<pre>Jiangshi Cat
Horror movie maniac, or real g-g-ghost?
Mystic seal is just this month's gas bill…
Cheap to produce, 100% survives once!</pre>
**Masai Cat's description was entirely unchanged.
*The symbol written in the middle of Jiangshi Cat's talisman is 二 above a 2. The symbol also translates to 2.
*The Masai (pronounced mas-eye) is an ethnic group in Kenya, which is well-known for their jumping tribal dance.
*Jiangshi(僵尸) refers to a type of stiff (jiang), reanimated corpse in Chinese folklore, sometimes called "hopping vampires" by those unfamiliar with the concept. The main feature of a Jiangshi is hopping around while dressed in Qing dynasty garments and having a paper seal on the head. They are said to appear at night and kill people by sucking out their life force (qi), then return to their graves as they fear sunlight, like vampires. They are also similar in how they are countered by a specific type of plant, being the peach tree instead of garlic. Other details are often disputed and vary from source to source.
*Masai Cat is supposed to have a fourth stripe among the ones around its legs, but it was mostly removed when its sprites were being compressed. The stripe is visible in some high [[Media:037 c HD.png|high resolution]] renders of it, however.
*Pogo Cat has his very own game in the form of [[Go! Go! Pogo Cat]].

